    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " API provides the underlying basis for Spring’s IoC functionality. Its specific contracts are mostly used in integration with other parts of Spring and related third-party frameworks, and its "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultListableBeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " implementation is a key delegate within the higher-level "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "GenericApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " container."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and related interfaces (such as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactoryAware"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "InitializingBean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DisposableBean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") are important integration points for other framework components. By not requiring any annotations or even reflection, they allow for very efficient interaction between the container and its components. Application-level beans may use the same callback interfaces but typically prefer declarative dependency injection instead, either through annotations or through programmatic configuration."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note that the core "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " API level and its "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultListableBeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " implementation do not make assumptions about the configuration format or any component annotations to be used. All of these flavors come in through extensions (such as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "XmlBeanDefinitionReader"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AutowiredAnnotationBeanPostProcessor"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") and operate on shared "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanDefinition"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " objects as a core metadata representation. This is the essence of what makes Spring’s container so flexible and extensible."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This section explains the differences between the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " container levels and the implications on bootstrapping."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You should use an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " unless you have a good reason for not doing so, with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "GenericApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and its subclass "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AnnotationConfigApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " as the common implementations for custom bootstrapping. These are the primary entry points to Spring’s core container for all common purposes: loading of configuration files, triggering a classpath scan, programmatically registering bean definitions and annotated classes, and (as of 5.0) registering functional bean definitions."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Because an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " includes all the functionality of a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", it is generally recommended over a plain "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", except for scenarios where full control over bean processing is needed. Within an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (such as the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "GenericApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " implementation), several kinds of beans are detected by convention (that is, by bean name or by bean type — in particular, post-processors), while a plain "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultListableBeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is agnostic about any special beans."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "For many extended container features, such as annotation processing and AOP proxying, the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "BeanPostProcessor"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " extension point"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "core/beans/factory-extension.html#beans-factory-extension-bpp"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is essential. If you use only a plain "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultListableBeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", such post-processors do not get detected and activated by default. This situation could be confusing, because nothing is actually wrong with your bean configuration. Rather, in such a scenario, the container needs to be fully bootstrapped through additional setup."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following table lists features provided by the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BeanFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interfaces and implementations."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
